 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you these days? Try a two step mix trick with two thin layers of moisturizer instead one thick one. Or use thin layer of gel with a light lipstick on top. Use a moisturiser that matches your skin type, or a small amount of oil from your fingers. For darker skin, using light lipstick gives a glowy effect. Mixing several shades in one brush gives random shade blending without the tool clutter. Or use a small brush for each shade. Brush lines can be filled with the lip pencil, or you can use your lipstick on one side and swipe it across the lips for a brushed effect.",
